    "conclusion": "these ARE functions of the program, so these \u2014 never a cycle count \u2014 are what a cost model may be fitted to and what a compiler comparison may be made on. `matmul` (issued) is NOT one of them: it counts the retry-spin an operand-starved core performs, so it is a stall meter wearing a work meter's name, and reading it as work is how a stall gets mistaken for a workload."
